<mujoco model="kid_RL_dance">
  <!--
    CAD export of the 4-axis-arm Kid_RL_v3 revision
    (kid_RL_v3_description/urdf/kid_RL.xml), with the conventions the exporter
    does not emit re-applied by hand so the training config keeps working:

      1. meshdir "../meshes" -> "assets" (meshes vendored next to this file).
      2. Arm joints/actuators renamed l_*/r_* -> left_*/right_*, and bodies
         torso -> torso_1, {left,right}_shoulder -> *_shoulder_1, so the joint- and
         body-name regexes in tasks/ keep matching the old model's convention.
      3. Restored the left_foot/right_foot sites (FOOT_HEIGHT_SCAN_CFG raycasts
         from them; without them the scene fails to build).
      4. group="1" on every collision geom, and "<body>_self_collision_<n>" names
         on the unnamed proxy boxes. The foot height scan uses
         include_geom_groups=(0,) to mean "terrain only", so any collision geom
         left in group 0 gets hit by its own rays.
      5. armature="1e-3" on the 8 passive linkage joints (*_roll_cap and
         *_roll_actual); the export ships 5e-8 / nothing.

    Everything else -- legs, pelvis/ankle 4-bar linkages, tendons, equalities,
    contact excludes, sensors, motor default classes -- is the export verbatim.
    Upper-body collision is intentionally the CAD mesh, not primitive proxies.
  -->
